{"title":"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The volume of a certain rectangular solid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cm<sup>3</sup>, its total surface area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm<sup>2</sup>, and its three dimensions are in geometric progression. The sums of the lengths in cm of all the edges of this solid is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9c5316ad032ba09c7a0fb06275ddb5a2fe21789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ } 28 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }32 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\  } 36 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\  } 40 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\  }44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"388\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As the dimensions are in geometric progression, let them be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/419c5f8d297aea1d10ae603202d0b1cdcfdbeac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/3/87313d2c0eb7231875c80e25357084ea067e0545.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$br$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> cm, so the volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/8/9b87b5e7bf2a2fc46f8de62037ddc3e994462a9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{b}{r}\\right)(b)(br) = b^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"136\" height=\"45\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/3/3932470957c50d2ca44241de051157711bdaa2c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^3 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197213da9d06b2c5b59a10ad17f6a4aeb43d6697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. The surface area condition now yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/6/01677d15277ceaa565675d60900d12869f04648c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}2\\left(\\frac{2}{r}\\right)(2)+2(2)(2r)+2(2r)\\left(\\frac{2}{r}\\right) = 32 &amp;\\iff \\frac{8}{r}+8+8r = 32 \\\\ &amp;\\iff r+\\frac{1}{r} = 3 \\\\ &amp;\\iff r^2-3r+1 = 0 \\\\ &amp;\\iff r = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{5}}{2}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"491\" height=\"162\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/9/c2945daa5a807f307f279f2b3241f1bfbb2bb4c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3-\\sqrt{5}}{2} = \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{3+\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\right)},\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"58\" /> the two possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> do not actually give different dimensions, but merely determine whether they are in increasing or decreasing order. Therefore, without loss of generality, we take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/0/b00aa62f82985bd9007691fa054c9addaf96c936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{3+\\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"43\" />, giving the dimensions (in cm) as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35ade854b5f1b4411412cfeb29205a8c64c70982.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}&amp;\\frac{2}{\\left(\\frac{3+\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\right)}, 2, \\text{ and } 2\\left(\\frac{3+\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{4}{3+\\sqrt{5}}, 2, \\text{ and } 3+\\sqrt{5} \\\\ &amp;= 3-\\sqrt{5}, 2, \\text{ and } 3+\\sqrt{5}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"220\" height=\"136\" />\n</p><p>As there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> edges with each of these distinct lengths, it follows that the sum of all the edge lengths (in cm) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02cab39294444f7651110bad786ca355b41792cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}4\\left(3-\\sqrt{5}+2+3+\\sqrt{5}\\right) &amp;= 4(8) \\\\ &amp;= \\boxed{\\text{(B)} \\ 32}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"285\" height=\"67\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similarly to in Solution 1, we let the dimensions (in cm) be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/3/87313d2c0eb7231875c80e25357084ea067e0545.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$br$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/3039d3d86bb8a684dd65f4b7f04d0a1db189dbc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$br^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"17\" />, so that the volume condition gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93dd916e460c389a9cde93155eeb7a5a5dd4584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 = b^3r^3 = (br)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"21\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a21e14362fe6087c93688adcc185b71482caedf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$br = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. The surface area condition now becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f7880ccbaf6e726197a13668af11a04820d46d7c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}2(b)(br)+2(br)\\left(br^2\\right)+2\\left(br^2\\right)(b) = 32 &amp;\\iff b^2r+b^2r^2+b^2r^3 = 16 \\\\&amp;\\iff br\\left(b+br+br^2\\right) = 16,\\end{align*}\" width=\"537\" height=\"49\" /> so substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a21e14362fe6087c93688adcc185b71482caedf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$br = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> from above immediately gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/b/14b79ec751d7563bc560a93e346680eaa3e1913c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b+br+br^2 = \\frac{16}{2} = 8,\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"37\" /> and hence, without needing to actually compute the dimensions, we deduce that the sum of the edge lengths (in cm) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/7/2575762bbc48bacba358d26ca4211f6cd16ba70d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4b + 4br + 4br^2 = 4(8) = \\boxed{\\text{(B)} \\ 32}.\\]\" width=\"263\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME\" title=\"1985 AHSME\">1985 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1985 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174847\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 196/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5243/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.363      1 -total\n 57.67%    7.130      1 Template:AHSME_box\n 39.68%    4.906      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10322:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174847 and revision id 217174. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}